          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is commonly known as
            %em Minkowski’s inequality
            is the statement that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} p-norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                  %mo ≔
                  %mroot
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                      %mi d
                      %mi μ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert f\Vert_p} \coloneqq \root{p}{\int_X {\vert f\vert^p} d\mu}
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+spaces"} Lebesgue spaces
            indeed satisfies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"} triangle inequality
          %h2#proofs Proofs
          %p
            Our proof of Minkowski’s inequality is broken down into a few simple lemmas. The plan is to boil it down to two things: the scaling axiom, and convexity of the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto {|x|^p}
            (as a function from real or complex numbers to nonnegative real numbers).
          %p
            First, some generalities. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a (real or complex) vector space equipped with a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|(-)\|}\colon V \to [0, \infty]
            that satisfies the scaling axiom:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi t
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t v\|} = {|t|} \, {\|v\|}
            for all scalars
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|v\|} = 0
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+ball"} unit ball
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v \in V \;|\; {\|v\|} \leq 1\}.
          #conditions.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p Given that the scaling and separation axioms hold, the following conditions are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li The triangle inequality is satisfied.
              %li
                The unit ball is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|u\|} = {\|v\|} = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi t
                        %mi u
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t u + (1-t)v\|} \leq 1
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0, 1]
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since conditions 2. and 3. are pretty obviously equivalent, we just prove 1. and 3. are equivalent. Condition 1. implies condition 3. easily: if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|u\| = 1 = \|v\|
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi t
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq t \leq 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi t
                              %mi u
                              %mo +
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi t
                              %mi u
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo +
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi u
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    {\|t u + (1-t)v\|} &amp; \leq &amp; {\|t u\|} + {\|(1-t)v\|} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; t {\|u\|} + (1-t) {\|v\|} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; t + (1-t) = 1.}
            %p
              Now we prove that 3. implies 1. Suppose
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ,
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|v\|}, {\|v'\|} \in (0, \infty)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = \frac{v}{{\|v\|}}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' = \frac{v'}{{\|v'\|}}
              be the associated unit vectors. Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi v
                                %mo +
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                              %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mo +
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo ′
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mo )
                            %mfrac
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mi v
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo +
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mo +
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                    %mi v
                                    %mo ′
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mo )
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mi u
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi u
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\frac{v + v'}{{\|v\|}+{\|v'\|}} &amp; = &amp; \left(\frac{{\|v\|}}{{\|v\|}+{\|v'\|}}\right)\frac{v}{{\|v\|}} + \left(\frac{{\|v'\|}}{{\|v\|}+{\|v'\|}}\right)\frac{v'}{{\|v'\|}} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; t u + (1-t)u'}
            %p
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mo +
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = \frac{{\|v\|}}{{\|v\|} + {\|v'\|}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi t
                      %mi u
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t u + (1-t)u'\|} \leq 1
            %p but by the scaling axiom, this is the same as saying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{{\|v + v'\|}}{{\|v\|} + {\|v'\|}} \leq 1,
            %p which is the triangle inequality.
          %p
            Consider now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            with its
            = succeed "-norm" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|} = {|f|_p}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#conditions"}
          %ul
            %li
              %strong Condition 4:
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi u
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                        %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|u|_{p}^{p}} = 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi v
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                          %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|v|_{p}^{p}} = 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi t
                      %mi u
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi v
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                        %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|t u + (1-t)v|_{p}^{p}} \leq 1
              whenever
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi t
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq t \leq 1
          %p
            This allows us to remove the cumbersome exponent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/p
            in the definition of the
            = succeed "-norm." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          #convex.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{R}
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x) = |x|^p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is convex, i.e., for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi t
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi y
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|t x + (1-t)y|^p} \leq t{|x|^p} + (1-t){|y|^p}
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0, 1]
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: x \mapsto {|x|}
              is convex, and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \lt p
              the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi t
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: t \mapsto t^p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \geq 0
              is monotone increasing and convex, by the first and second derivative tests. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi t
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(t x + (1-t)y) \leq t g(x) + (1-t)g(y)
              and then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi t
                            %mi x
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi t
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    f(g(t x + (1-t)y)) &amp; \leq &amp; f(t g(x) + (1-t)g(y)) \\
                    \&amp; \leq &amp; t f(g(x)) + (1-t)f(g(y))
                    }
            %p
              so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g: x \mapsto {|x|^p}
              is convex.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_minkowskis_inequality Proof of Minkowski’s inequality
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              be unit vectors in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi t
                      %mi u
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi v
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                        %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|t u + (1-t)v|_p^p} \leq 1
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0, 1]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi t
                      %mi u
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi v
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi X
                    %mi t
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_X {|t u + (1-t)v|^p} \,d\mu \leq \int_X t{|u|}^p + (1-t){|v|}^p \,d\mu
            %p
              by Lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#convex"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi u
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi v
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int {|u|^p} = 1 = \int {|v|^p}
          %p
            Another commonly seen proof of Minkowski’s inequality derives it with the help of
